msgid "This information is superceded by :ref:`common-landing-gear`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/landing-gear.rst:7 08fe379dd2b04ec3bdebd09123cbe8d1
msgid "Archived: Landing Gear"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/landing-gear.rst:9 6f9cfaa2b7dc40e8b02ba548e494ad40
msgid ""
"Copter supports retractable Landing Gear activated by a servo mechanism "
"(like these sold by `Hobby King <https://hobbyking.com/en_us/quanum-600"
"-class-quick-release-universal-retractable-gear-set-680uc-pro-hexa-"
"copter.html?___store=en_us>`__). The gear can be manually "
"retracted/deployed with an auxiliary switch. The gear will also "
"automatically deploy during landing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/landing-gear.rst:14 d36fd19503dd46798fa5b1eb6751e33e
msgid ""
"There is some simple logic controlling the operation beyond simply "
"responding to retract/deploy commands from the controller.  If the system"
" is booted up and the landing gear control switch is in the retract "
"position, the landing gear will not retract.  This is done to prevent "
"damage to the landing gear or airframe should the switch be accidentally "
"left in the retract position on start-up.  In this case, the landing gear"
" will not retract until the switch is first moved to the deploy position,"
" and then back to the retract position."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/landing-gear.rst:23 a1548ea585804890b0662dfcff2c33ab
msgid ""
"The landing gear will automatically deploy when the flight mode is "
"changed to Land, during the final landing phase of RTL mode, and when a "
"Land command is executed in AUTO mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/landing-gear.rst:28 a3785405c96643cab3c7a4198a62c938
msgid "Support for landing gear was introduced in AC 3.3"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/landing-gear.rst:34 88b03d42d1a54b71be164d445d20327c
msgid "Connecting to the Pixhawk"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/landing-gear.rst:36 bec7a054796a432c97645c76b22b77f4
msgid ""
"Most retractable landing gear will require just a single PWM cable to "
"connected to one of the AUX outputs on the back of the Pixhawk (AUX1 ~ "
"AUX4)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/landing-gear.rst:45 f7aad71c1dc64922a4959a5e74ee2ec4
msgid ""
"The signal wire (usually white) should be connected to the lower most "
"\"S\" pin."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/landing-gear.rst:48 d67b998b7de04d918908cd2c7c522cc7
msgid "Setup through the Mission Planner"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/landing-gear.rst:50 46cbc380b92a4cfa9676bf3b5f1f162c
msgid ""
"Use the Mission Planner's Full Parameter List (or equivalent) to set the "
"following parameters:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/landing-gear.rst:53 53230762ee6549b2b655d3ac345534d3
msgid ""
"If using AC3.5 (or higher) set ``SERVOn_FUNCTION to 29`` \"Landing "
"Gear\", where **n** is the number for the connected servo (e.g. "
":ref:`SERVO9_FUNCTION <SERVO9_FUNCTION>` for AUX1, :ref:`SERVO10_FUNCTION"
" <SERVO10_FUNCTION>` for AUX2 etc.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/landing-gear.rst:55 30ab095d389844608320eadbd847f8e9
msgid ""
"If using AC3.4.6 (or lower) set ``RCn_FUNCTION to 29`` \"Landing Gear\", "
"where **n** is the number for the connected servo (e.g. ``RC9_FUNCTION "
"<RC9_FUNCTION>`` for AUX1, ``RC10_FUNCTION <RC10_FUNCTION>`` for AUX2 "
"etc.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/landing-gear.rst:56 b84311f598b44f6ab640285808bf252a
msgid ""
"``LGR_SERVO_DEPLOY <LGR_SERVO_DEPLOY>`` — servo PWM value required to "
"deploy the landing gear."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/landing-gear.rst:58 952ddac906fe419b9e54947cb90b9ae7
msgid ""
"``LGR_SERVO_RTRACT <LGR_SERVO_RTRACT>`` — servo PWM value required to "
"retract the landing gear."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/landing-gear.rst:64 574cbd7a1e2943e684f0f516ecc40940
msgid "MissionPlanner: Landing Gear Configuration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/landing-gear.rst:66 b7de23807d5748709ce369a808b958c1
msgid ""
"Set an :ref:`auxiliary switch <channel-7-and-8-options>` to \"Landing "
"Gear\" in order to enable manual control (i.e. set CH7_OPT or CH8_OPT to "
"\"29\")"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/landing-gear.rst:68 cb9339fb87f84387a39e3a5f545c67f3
msgid ""
"When the switch is in the \"low\" position the gear will be deployed, "
"\"high\" will be retracted, \"middle\" is a neutral position that will "
"not change the gear's state."
msgstr ""

